n but did not specify form.\\\" ,\n    \"significance\": \"minor\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"section-name\": \"Part 2 - 6. GENERAL CONDITIONS (Collection and Disclosure of Information)\",\n    \"document-a-text\": \\\"6.5. Collection of Information. ... may need to obtain certain information, such as property identification information, property zoning or other land use information, GST number, information to establish compliance with Minimum Required Domestic Content Level, and information to establish that the Supplier is an Eligible Participant from third parties...\\\\nDisclosure of Information. OPA may disclose to LDC and the Ministry of Energy, and certain other Ontario government ministries, certain information ... including without limitation, Supplier’s name, facility location, microFIT Program eligibility characteristics, compliance with Minimum Required Domestic Content Level, Supplier’s electricity generation, pricing and payments.\\\",\n    \"document-b-text\": \\\"6.5. Collection of Information. ... may need to obtain certain information, such as property identification information, property zoning or other land use information, GST number, and information to establish that the Supplier is an Eligible Participant from third parties...\\\\nDisclosure of Information. OPA may disclose to LDC and the Ministry of Energy, and certain other Ontario government ministries, certain information ... including without limitation, Supplier’s name, facility location, microFIT Program eligibility characteristics, Supplier’s electricity generation, pricing and payments. The OPA may disclose certain information, including the details of the Facility and location of the Facility, to other government ministries, agencies, institutions or organizations, for purposes of promoting public health and safety and allowing emergency services personnel, as well as other public officials to plan and respond properly in the event of an emergency.\\\",\n    \"difference-summary\": \\\"Version 3.1.1 removes explicit references to collecting or disclosing information about compliance with the Minimum Required Domestic Content Level. Version 3.1.1 also adds a new explicit basis/recipient for disclosure (other ministries/agencies/institutions) for public health/safety and emergency planning purposes. These are substantive changes to data collection and disclosure terms.\\\",\n    \"significance\": \"major\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"section-name\": \"Part 2 - 6.6 Statement Copies and 6.7 Supplier Verification\",\n    \"document-a-text\": \\\"6.6. Statement Copies. Supplier shall, at the request of OPA, provide OPA with copies of all settlement statements, invoices and all other correspondence between Supplier and LDC relating to the Facility or any Generation Payment ...\\\\n6.7. Supplier Verification and use of a Representative. Supplier acknowledges and agrees that OPA may require Supplier to provide instructions, requests or decisions in order to terminate, amend or assign ...\\\",\n    \"document-b-text\": \\\"6.6. Statement Copies. Supplier shall, at the request of OPA, provide OPA with copies of all settlement statements, invoices and all other correspondence between Supplier and LDC relating to the Facility or any Generation Payment ...\\\\n6.7. Supplier Verification and use of a Representative. Supplier acknowledges and agrees that OPA may require Supplier to provide instructions, requests or decisions in order to terminate, amend or assign ...\\\",\n    \"difference-summary\": \"These clauses appear substantively identical in the provided extracts.\",\n    \"significance\": \"identical\"\n  }\n]",
