    "The principal change from Version 2.0 to Version 3.1.1 is the removal of the Minimum Required Domestic Content Level and all contract references obligating the Supplier to warrant or support verification of such domestic content. This is a material change affecting supplier obligations, program eligibility enforcement, and any downstream use of domestic content as a selection or compliance criterion. Additionally, v3.1.1 introduces a requirement that certain notifications be made \"in the Prescribed Form\" (operational change) and expands permitted data disclosures to include other government bodies for public health, safety and emergency planning (privacy and data-sharing impact). Counsel and program administrators should confirm whether these changes reflect intended policy updates, and privacy/compliance teams should review the expanded disclosure language."}},
